.TH AD 1 "2026-08-30" "ad 2.0" "ad animator"
.SH NAME
ad \- standalone terminal animation engine (reads timed op stream, animates in terminal)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad
.RI [ options ]
.I <oldfile>
< timed_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad
is the terminal animation engine. It reads a timed V2 TSV op stream from stdin and applies each op to the buffer, rendering the transformation to the terminal. Every op carries its own (line, col); the animator moves the cursor to that position before applying the op.
.PP
This is the C implementation (preferred). A Perl fallback exists at
animator/perl/ad.pl.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-display
Process without rendering (write snapshot only). Useful for testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed  N
Speed multiplier (0.5=half, 2=double, 5=5x). Default: 1.0.
.TP
.BI \-\-snapshot  FILE
Write the final buffer state to FILE.
.TP
.BI \-\-output  FILE
Write the buffer to FILE after each op (for debugging).
.TP
.BI \-\-colormap\-old  FILE
Load syntax colors for the old file (from ad_colorize).
.TP
.BI \-\-colormap\-new  FILE
Load syntax colors for the new file.
.TP
.BI \-\-scroll  MODE
Scroll mode: zz (center), zt (top), zb (bottom), none. Default: zz.
.TP
.B \-\-diff\-stat
Show diff stat overlay (X/Y lines changed).
.TP
.B \-\-diff\-highlight
Highlight changed lines green/red.
.TP
.B \-\-bell
Ring terminal bell on error (cursor clamped to buffer bounds).
.TP
.BI \-\-tick\-ms  N
Animation frame interval in ms. Default: 16 (~60fps).
.TP
.BI \-\-seek  N
Start animation at op N (apply ops 0..N silently, then animate from N).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-line\-len  N
Skip char-level diff for lines > N chars. Default: 1048576 (1MB).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print debug info to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Process ops without rendering (for timing tests).
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-V
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
During animation (interactive mode), these keys are active:
.TP
.B Space
Pause / resume.
.TP
.B n
Skip current hunk (apply instantly, move to next).
.TP
.B b
Back to previous hunk (revert and restart).
.TP
.B q
Stop animation (leave buffer in current state).
.TP
.B +
Speed up (x1.5).
.TP
.B -
Slow down (x0.67).
.TP
.B =
Reset speed to 1.0x.
.TP
.B ?
Show in-vim help.
.SH INPUT FORMAT
The timed op stream is V2 TSV (tab-separated, 1-indexed line/col):
.PP
.RS
.nf
# diffvim timed ops v2
HUNK\\t<target>\\t<del>\\t<ins>\\t<end_ins>\\t<end_del>
keep\\t<line>\\t<col>\\t<code>\\t<char_repr>
delete\\t<line>\\t<col>\\t<code>\\t<char_repr>
insert\\t<line>\\t<col>\\t<code>\\t<char_repr>
delay\\t<ms>\\t<type>
HUNK_END
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. Use CLI flags or the config file at
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ad/config.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad --no-display --speed 1000 --snapshot out.txt old.py < timed.txt
Animate fast, write result to out.txt.
.TP
.B ad --speed 0.5 old.py < timed.txt
Slow animation for presentations.
.TP
.B ad --diff-stat --diff-highlight old.py < timed.txt
Show diff stats and highlight changed lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_pipeline (1),
.BR ad_vim (1),
.BR ad_postprocess (1)
